# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# ⚠️ THIS FILE CANNOT ENFORCE THE BLOCKLIST BELOW. Cloudflare Pages serves a
# matching static asset FIRST and only consults _redirects when nothing matches,
# so every rule here that names a file which actually exists has never fired.
# Measured in production 2026-08-21: /CLAUDE.md, /PROGRESS.md, /RELEASES.md,
# /palette-guide.html, /tests/*, /scripts/*, /tools/* all answered 200 with
# their real content. The only entries that 404'd were /eval/* and
# /copywriting/*, whose files are not deployed at all — the list worked exactly
# where it was not needed.
#
# functions/_middleware.js is what actually denies these paths; Functions run
# before asset resolution. This file is kept in step so the two do not
# disagree, and tests/private-files.mjs asserts both.

#
# PROGRESS.md (dev log), the AUDIT-*.md findings, and CLAUDE.md (the working
# brief for the agents on this repo) live here for contributors, but must not
# be part of the public site. An audit in particular is a list of this site's
# weak points with reproduction steps — the last thing to leave reachable.
# Serve a 404 for them instead of handing the file to visitors.
/PROGRESS.md   /404.html   404
/AUDIT-*.md    /404.html   404
/CLAUDE.md     /404.html   404
/RELEASES.md   /404.html   404
/ARCHITECTURE.md   /404.html   404
/OVERVIEW.md   /404.html   404

# The instruction stack is the product. Generated decks under copywriting/ are
# verbatim copies of it and are gitignored, but this directory is inside the
# served tree — so anything that lands here by accident (a stray regeneration
# before a deploy) would be public. Serve a 404 for the whole directory.
/copywriting/*   /404.html   404

# Development directories. None of these are part of the site, and eval/ in
# particular drives the prompt engine — a harness is a map of what it tests.
/eval/*          /404.html   404
/tests/*         /404.html   404
/scripts/*       /404.html   404
/artifacts/*     /404.html   404
/tools/*         /404.html   404

# Internal colour references. palette-guide and palette-overview exist to show
# the raw ramps to whoever is editing them; they are the one place where naked
# hex is correct, and they are not part of the product.
/palette-guide.html      /404.html   404
/palette-overview.html   /404.html   404

# Retired visual experiments must not remain publicly reachable.
/baoxianghua-compositions.html   /404.html   404
